  "around": {
    "note": "The same trip when the host can open a window around the message (a timeline view opened with an anchor) instead of paging back to it. The loop: ask the list for `anchor.messageId`, so a message already on screen opens nothing; otherwise call `openAround(anchor)` once — it answers the anchor key, the row key the list will draw the message with, or nothing (null, empty or blank) when the message is not in the history; then settle and ask the list for that key up to `settleAttempts` times. `isCurrent` is checked before every ask, before opening, after opening and before every settle, and `cancelled` ends the trip silently. A shown message is scrolled to and marked by the list itself. Each case scripts one run: `loaded` means the list already has the message; `openAnswer` is what the host answers; the list finds the key from the `drawnFromShow`-th ask on (counting the first ask); `cancelAfterShows` turns `isCurrent` false after that many asks; `cancelAfterOpen` turns it false once the host has answered. `expected` counts the host calls and the asks, and lists the id of every ask in order; the anchor handed to the host is the one given, unchanged.",
